    "mechanism": {
      "description": "Pi mechanism is one closed source-neutral event class. realize is a generic representation-only stage when no more specific class applies. One realize instance anchored directly to a J.signature handle or C slot may be discharged by that parameter binding and its direct routed use; it does not require an identity assignment. Multiple instances anchored to the same handle still denote distinct routed use-sites/stages. address_base is an independently compiler-visible, program-uniform pointer/base or integer base-address contribution before lane merge; Lift uses it only when that separate source stage exists. address_lane is the compiler-visible stage that forms the lane-varying contribution or final address. When routes contain address_base -> address_lane, Replay must materialize two distinct stages in that order and must not algebraically fold them into one flat vector offset; these are address-contribution roles and do not require two pointer-add instructions. transfer_direct and transfer_async classify data movement after address formation; update_atomic and update_privatized classify physical update realization; synchronize classifies synchronization. Region placement='program' only scopes an instance to one program; it does not assert that a program/grid coordinate is read. A compiler-visible program/grid coordinate is a separate realization stage and requires its own realize instance and routes. Its source-neutral encoding is a realize instance anchored to the corresponding J domain in a program region whose scalar dependency path enters address_base before transfer; a domain/C dependency path entering address_lane is lane-varying instead. Replay must preserve this base-versus-lane distinction and U_f maps it to public frontend APIs. Integer coordinate arithmetic is a realize stage; address_base and address_lane classify where its program-uniform and lane-varying paths enter address formation rather than relabeling every arithmetic op. If Source visibly forms a separable program-uniform integer base and a lane offset, then merges them before one pointer addition, the program path still enters address_base and routes to address_lane. Replay preserves both integer stages but does not require a second pointer addition. Only a Source with no separable program-uniform contribution uses a lone address_lane stage. Replay must not invent program_id, a grid offset, or an affine address stage from region placement, grid convention, or C alone. Address classes never carry an index/offset formula, constant, integer width, cast, dtype, shape, vector length, predicate, fill, frontend API, or logical access semantics.",
      "enum": [
        "realize",
        "address_base",
        "address_lane",
        "transfer_direct",
        "transfer_async",
        "update_atomic",
        "update_privatized",
        "synchronize"
      ],
      "type": "string"
    },
